      "side": 1,
      "message": "So far I have gone over:\n\n* `SkBmpRustCodec.h` and `SkBmpRustCodec.cpp`: see the comments below\n* `SkBmpRustDecoder.h` and `SkBmpRustDecoder.cpp`: LGTM\n\n-------------------\n\nI also have looked more closely at the option of reusing the BMP decoder from [the `image` crate](https://docs.rs/image).  I apologize for not doing this earlier (ideally before our previous meeting where we tentatively concluded to try a new codec implementation).  FWIW the size of this CL has been a strong motivator for re-considering reusing the `image` crate.\n\nI understand that if we (hypothetically) decide to reverse this decision, then this may result in some unfortunate churn.  The reversal may:\n\n* Invalidate some (but definitely not all) work that you have put into this CL\n* Make some of my code review feedback below non-applicable anymore\n\nWith the disclaimers out of the way, let me try to go over the gaps that [the design doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fc7KI1AhvCOLZhAStg_jIQLlCA3aCZP4vhgFlLn1ZTk/edit?tab\u003dt.0#heading\u003dh.fy7bc7pfp9fa) has identified in the `image` crate:\n\n\u003e Streaming decode not supported\n\n- For PNG this was also missing - we also had to add this in https://github.com/image-rs/image-png/pull/496\n- AFAICT `SkBmpCodec.cpp` only returns `kIncompleteInput` from `SkBmpCodec::ReadHeader` (i.e. doesn’t support streaming decoding of actual pixels).  If this is indeed the case, then maybe initially `SkBmpRustCodec` may ignore streaming and just implement/override `SkCodec::onGetPixels`.  This doesn\u0027t reduce the overall amount of work (since to replicate `blink::BMPImageDecoder`\u0027s functionality we would still need streaming support I think), but splitting the work into smaller CL seems desirable.\n\n\u003e JPEG/PNG encoding: not supported\n\nFWIW https://crbug.com/456842524 proposes to remove Chromium support for JPEG/PNG-embedded-in-BMP.\n\n\u003e OS/2 Advanced Formats: HUFFMAN1D, RLE24 not supported\n\u003e Color management: Color space info, ICC profiles not supported\n\u003e BITMAPARRAY (filetype 0x4241 - “BA” -multiple BMPs in one file) not supported (only file type 0x424D - “BM” is supported, see).\n\nAck.\n\nI note that the public API for accessing the ICC profile already exists, except that `image::codecs::bmp::BmpDecoder` indeed doesn\u0027t implement the `icc_profile` accessor from the `ImageDecoder` trait.\n\nI think the main question here would be about the cost of contributing (+maintaining!) these features 1) in a new library VS 2) in the `image` crate.\n\n\u003e seems far from having a full test coverage\n\nAck.\n\nThis particular gap seems fairly easy to address - IIUC there is already an end-to-end test that tries to decode all the images from https://github.com/image-rs/image/tree/main/tests/images/bmp.  So maybe things would auto-magically work if we just added images from the BMP test suite to that directory?",
      "revId": "cc6e7f648b2c05b805a99333be3bfdfea2dcc491",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
