      "side": 1,
      "message": "[`blink::SegmentStream`]() can initially contain only a partial input (e.g. when only a part of a HTTP response has been received).  In this case:\n\n* `SkPngRustDecoder::MakeFromStream` succeeds, and when/if `codec-\u003eincrementalDecode` returns `kIncompleteInput`, then the caller can retry after more data is available through the original input stream.\n* IIUC `SkBmpRustCodec::MakeFromStream` returns `kIncompleteInput`.  This means that when `SkiaImageDecoderBase::OnSetData` receives more data, then it has to retry parsing the BMP from scratch (i.e. calling `OnCreateSkCodec` again, potentially copying the same pixels again).\n\nThe behavior of `SkBmpRustCodec` seems functionally correct, but it\u0027s probably desirable to match what the legacy `blink::BMPImageReader` is doing and supporting streaming/incremental decoding.  FWIW we don\u0027t need to copy the approach of `blink::BMPImageReader` which tracks how far the image has been decoded via [`decoded_offset_`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/image-decoders/bmp/bmp_image_reader.h;l\u003d323-324;drc\u003d35d26d364efb57d0386b98312ba739f7f65ae97e) and [`coord_`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/image-decoders/bmp/bmp_image_reader.h;l\u003d379-380;drc\u003d35d26d364efb57d0386b98312ba739f7f65ae97e) - we can do something different.  One approach here would be to reuse [`ReadAndSeekTraitsAdapterForSkStream`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/codec/SkPngRustCodec.cpp;l\u003d306-308;drc\u003d5658e91de531f3a05ebb87fad3deed5da7ecb5b2) from `SkPngRustCodec.cpp`.  If we decide to try this route, then I think it would be useful to try and move this part of code into `skia/common/rust`:\n\n* `ReadAndSeekTraitsAdapterForSkStream` in `common/SkStreamAdapter.h` and `SkStreamAdapter.cpp`\n* `skia/rust/png/FFI.h` \u003d\u003e `common/SkStreamAdapterInterfaces.h`\n* I/O-trait-related parts of `skia/rust/png/FFI.rs` \u003d\u003e `io_traits_ffi.rs`\n* Adjust `#[cxx::bridge]` as needed - most likely using techniques from https://cxx.rs/extern-c++.html#safely-unifying-occurrences-of-an-extern-type-across-bridges",
